#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kpilot; Main Window Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the usage of &kpilot;'s main window and its menu "
"structure. The main window of &kpilot; also contains the &HotSync;-log, "
"which can be useful when debugging problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the first start &kpilot; opens the configuration dialog which allows you "
"to adjust its settings and select and configure the conduits to be used. "
"Click the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button to switch to the &HotSync;-log, "
"as shown <link linkend=\"main-app\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The Main Window</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpilot; Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Main Window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Main Window</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main window contains the application menu, which we will deal with here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu contains the synchronization menu items. "
"Note that these items do not start the sync process, they only select what "
"the new sync will be. To really start it, you must press the &HotSync; "
"button on your &PalmPilot;'s cradle (or on the &handheld; itself, when there "
"is no cradle)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is not possible to cancel a sync operation once the request has been made."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information regarding the synchronization functionality, please "
"check the <link linkend=\"synchronization\">Synchronization Chapter</link> "
"of this handbook, where you can find detailed descriptions of the "
"synchronization methods and options offered by &kpilot;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>HotSync</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make the next sync a &HotSync;. For more information, please check the <link "
"linkend=\"sync-s\"> Syncing your &handheld; data</link> section of this "
"handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>FullSync</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(not available with all installations) Make the next sync a FullSync. For "
"more information, please check the <link linkend=\"sync-s\"> Syncing your "
"&handheld; data</link> section of this handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy Handheld to PC</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This runs all conduits and syncs all databases, but instead of merging the "
"information from both sources, it will copy the handheld data to the PC. "
"<emphasis>Use with care, as this option erases the changes you made in your "
"PC since the last sync</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy PC to Handheld</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This runs all conduits and syncs all databases, but instead of merging the "
"information from both sources, it will copy the PC data to the handheld. "
"<emphasis>Use with care, as this option erases the changes you made in your "
"handheld since the last sync</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quits &kpilot;, closing the main window and stopping the daemon if that "
"<link linkend=\"stopdaemononexit\">configuration option</link> is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu allows you to configure &kpilot; main "
"interface and fine-tune the synchronization process with the &handheld;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Statusbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this menu item to toggle &kpilot;'s status bar on and off, or in other "
"words, to show it if hidden, or to hide it if shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Toolbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this menu item to toggle &kpilot;'s toolbar on and off, or in other "
"words, to show it if hidden, or to hide it if shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s shortcut configuration dialog, allowing you change or "
"create key bindings, which are associations between actions (for example, "
"opening &kpilot;'s configuration dialog) and keys or key combinations (for "
"instance, <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>A</keycap></"
"keycombo>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s toolbar configuration dialog. This dialog lists all "
"actions available for use on the toolbar, and the actions currently "
"displayed, allowing you to add or remove actions, and move the actions which "
"already are on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure KPilot...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s configuration dialog, allowing you to match your "
"hardware with the configuration, so that &kpilot; can talk with your "
"&handheld;, and to configure the way &kpilot; synchronizes your &PalmPilot; "
"with your desktop applications (through conduits). The <link linkend="
"\"configure\"> Configuring &kpilot;</link> chapter of this handbook offers "
"detailed information about these configuration options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Built-in Applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select one of the Built in applications, just click its icon on "
"&kpilot;'s sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kpilot;'s Sidebar</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kpilot;'s Sidebar</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>&kpilot;'s Sidebar</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting one of the built-in applications will cause that application to "
"appear in &kpilot;'s main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The File Installer</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just hit the <guibutton>Add file...</guibutton> button to add a file to the "
"list. These files will be installed on your &PalmPilot; during the next "
"&HotSync;. If you choose not to install these files on the &PalmPilot;, just "
"hit <guibutton>Clear list</guibutton> to remove any pending files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The file installer application supports dragging and dropping into the files "
"to install area. They will be installed the next time you &HotSync;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An internal copy of the file is kept, so you can even drag and drop &URL;s "
"from &konqueror;!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The File Installer</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

